[node name="Rules" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Margin/VBoxContainer/Scroll"]
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
bbcode_enabled = true
fit_content = true
text = "[b]Goal[/b]
Sink the other player's whole fleet. Each side's fleet is hidden from the other.

[b]Setup[/b]
Each player spends 25 points on ships, then places them on their own side of the board: left or right of the dark middle column (no-man's-land). Ships can face any of six directions. Islands (orange) block ships; Coastal Batteries can only go on islands. Hover over or tap a ship in ship selection for its details.

[b]Turns[/b]
Players take turns on the same device; hand it over when the swap screen appears. You can watch a replay of the other player's attacks before your turn.
Each ship gets 4 action points (AP) a turn: forward 1, rotate 60° 2, reverse 4, and fire, special or secondary 2 each. A ship fires once a turn (the carrier twice). The dots above a ship are its AP left; ships with none turn grey. Next Ship picks the next ship that can still act, and End Turn ends your turn for the whole fleet.

[b]Abilities[/b]
Specials and secondaries have a cooldown in turns, shown on their button. They start the game cooling down and count down at the start of each of your turns. Passives (and drawbacks) always apply.

[b]Damage[/b]
Board markers: red is a hit, white a miss, black a ship sunk or destroyed, and half and half a hit that was stopped (armor, or a cruiser shooting it down). Hover over a hex for its history. Ships more than half damaged can't move. Hover over or tap an entry in the fleet panels to see each ship's damage.

[b]Revealing[/b]
Some actions show ships to the other player for a turn, drawn faded: Sonar Pulse, Recon Flight, and a Coastal Battery firing.

[b]Menu[/b]
Esc opens the menu: resume, start a new game, replay this game with the same fleets, or return to the title screen."

[node name="Back" type="Button" parent="Margin/VBoxContainer"]
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 4
text = "Back"

[connection signal="pressed" from="Margin/VBoxContainer/Back" to="." method="_on_back_pressed"]
